# FIX-STOP-01 v2 red — the four-branch regression against the retracted implementation

Baseline: the two source files restored from commit c53bea1 with git show
(packages/db/src/session-admission.ts, apps/worker/src/session-admission-reconciler.ts),
which is the "revocation gone means settled" implementation. The test file is the new one.

Date 2026-10-28. Host macOS arm64, Node v24.18.0, pnpm 9.15.0.
Database: throwaway postgres:16 container on an OS-assigned port, database
workpal_e2e_wt_verify_lifecycle_concurr_c57d79f7d1 from this worktree's agent:doctor plan;
each suite clones an isolated database from the migration template and drops it in afterAll.
Prerequisite: pnpm --filter @rakazo/db generate and prisma migrate deploy.
Command (identical for red and green):
  VERIFY_DATABASE=1 DATABASE_URL=postgresql://***:***@127.0.0.1:<port>/workpal_e2e_wt_verify_lifecycle_concurr_c57d79f7d1 \
    pnpm exec vitest run packages/db/src/stop-session-release.postgres.test.ts --no-file-parallelism
No real model, no scripted runtime: persistence layer only. Host paths replaced with <worktree>.

6 of 7 failed. The decisive one is branch 3, which fails with
  AssertionError: expected 'acquired' to be 'recovering'
i.e. the retracted implementation hands the session to a successor although nothing proved the
old execution exited or the session detached. That is the defect this branch exists to catch.

